Description: ARM: imx: add device-tree support for the i.MX21
 Commit 4b563a066611 ("ARM: imx: Remove imx21 support") removed the
 i.MX21 because it had only board-file support. Bring it back as a
 DT-only SoC, like the i.MX1 and i.MX27: the machine only sets the CPU
 type; the AVIC, timer and peripherals come from the device tree.
 .
 The prototype of the old imx21_init_early() is dropped from common.h;
 it has had no definition since that removal.
Author: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AI generated code]
Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Ee1gRFAS7tp8oLbvQ
